{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Sheol.</b> Both masculine and feminine. And behold, it was stirred and aroused." "<b>Rephaim.</b> They are the dead. It is possible that the alef is in place of a weak he." "<b>Chief ones of the earth.</b> They are the kings, in the sense of או תיש (Proverbs 30:31)." "<b>It raised up from their thrones.</b> They arose as though they were alive. And it is possible that it was the custom of the Babylonians to place thrones in the tombs of kings."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:43.363563841Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}